The setter is already a minimal inline wrapper around `SetFieldFLOAT32Value` with constant subfield arguments, so there is no redundant work to remove; keeping it identical preserves behavior and the compiler already inlines it into callers.

```cpp
    void SetTotalFractionalAscent(FIT_FLOAT32 totalFractionalAscent)
    {
        SetFieldFLOAT32Value(89, totalFractionalAscent, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```